# Overview

## Minikube

`minikube start`: Starts a local Kubernetes cluster

`minikube status`: Gets the status of a local Kubernetes cluster

`minikube unpause`: Unpause Kubernetes

`minikube delete --all`: Set flag to delete all profiles

`minikube service <deployment-name> --url`: Gives you a URL that's actually reachable from your host.

## Kubectl

`kubectl create -f <replicaset-definition.yaml>`: Used to create a replica set or any object in Kubernetes depending on the file we are providing as input.

- `-f` allows us to pass a file.

`kubectl get all` - see list of all objects created.

`kubectl apply -f .` - deploys an entire folder you are in. Must be in the working directory of the folder.

`kubectl delete -f .` - Removes all pods/services based on the working directory.

`cat <path/filename.txt>` - view files (Helps viewing definition files)

`kubectl scale deployment <deployment-app> --replicas=<num>` - Scales a pod to the desired amount.

